    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄκκον:</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμόν,</span> Id. :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄκταλλος</span></b>  (
			Boeot.
		), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>eye,</i> Hdn.Gr. <i><span class="en">
				2.559
			</span></i>, restored in <i><span class="en">
				Corinn.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				2.89
			</span></i>.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄπτιλλος.</span>
			(Derived by various suffixes from root <i>oq[uglide]-</i>
			'see' in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψομαι, ὄσσε, ὄσσομαι,
				ὀφθαλμός,</span> Lat. <i>oculus.</i>) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκκῦλαι:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὀκλάσαι, καὶ ἐπὶ τῶν
				πτερ&lt;ν&gt;ῶν καθέζεσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
